{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-102477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}^{″}(1,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y-2xy & x-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-102477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}y-2xy & x-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}],$ \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y-2xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x-{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-2xy)=-2y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-{x}^{2})=1-2x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-2xy)=1-2x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-{x}^{2})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2y & 1-2x \\\\ 1-2x & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(1,2).$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(1,2)=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-102477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7bb03c9a97a80a934eeb050314d775f797fa80674863257aabfac0318d9c116"} {"question" "q-102477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-102477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-102477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-163637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}10xy & 5{x}^{2}-2y\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-163637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}10xy & 5{x}^{2}-2y\\end{aligned}],$ \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=10xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=5{x}^{2}-2y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(10xy)=10y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5{x}^{2}-2y)=10x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(10xy)=10x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}-2y)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}10y & 10x \\\\ 10x & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-163637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7bb03c9a97a80a934eeb050314d775f797fa80674863257aabfac0318d9c116"} {"question" "q-163637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-163637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}10 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}20 & -5 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 \\\\ 10 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 20 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-163637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\