\\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(e-{e}^{2-x})=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2-x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7bb03c9a97a80a934eeb050314d775f797fa80674863257aabfac0318d9c116"} {"question" "q-81110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2-x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}e & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2-x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2-x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}-4y+1 & 3{y}^{2}-4x-1\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}-4y+1 & 3{y}^{2}-4x-1\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-4y+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3{y}^{2}-4x-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-4y+1)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2}-4x-1)=-4 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-4y+1)=-4\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{y}^{2}-4x-1)=6y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7bb03c9a97a80a934eeb050314d775f797fa80674863257aabfac0318d9c116"} {"question" "q-81009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2y & 4x \\\\ 4x & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6y\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4x \\\\ 4x & -4y\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2x & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6y & 4x \\\\ 4x & 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6y\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-163635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}^{″}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-163635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}],$ \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2})=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-163635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7bb03c9a97a80a934eeb050314d775f797fa80674863257aabfac0318d9c116"} {"question" "q-163635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-163635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-163635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}^{″}(-1,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)=(y-1)({x}^{2}-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}((y-1)({x}^{2}-1)) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}((y-1)({x}^{2}-1))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x(y-1) & {x}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x(y-1))=2(y-1)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-1)=2x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x(y-1))=2x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}2(y-1) & 2x \\\\ 2x & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(-1,2).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1,2)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7bb03c9a97a80a934eeb050314d775f797fa80674863257aabfac0318d9c116"} {"question" "q-81123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-81123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-80939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-80939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+xy)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+x)=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1 & -x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbfed8d5ac8aed714d4ee90c33fe3f8b1cc32d8d027b77c3470a7b5d68567dab"} {"question" "q-80939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070131/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c7bb03c9a97a80a934eeb050314d775f797fa80674863257aabfac0318d9c116"} {"question" "q-80939" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :